   "I've set up a tumour\u2013normal sarek run for patient NTC-TN-P1. Before it can go, I need you to confirm which sample is the tumour and which is the normal.\n\n**Tumour/normal pairing** (one samplesheet, 2 samples)\n\n| patient | sample | status | metadata |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NTC-TN-P1 | D.SEQ-261110NA-11 | **1 (tumour)** | Primary tumour tissue, colon, surgical resection, WGS |\n| NTC-TN-P1 | D.SEQ-261110NA-12 | **0 (normal)** | Blood (matched normal), pre-operative blood draw, WGS |\n\nBoth samples are paired-end 150 bp whole-genome sequencing from an Illumina NovaSeq 6000. The patient is female, so sex is set to XX.\n\n**Run settings**\n- **Reference:** the local Luria GRCh38 reference (`GATK.GRCh38/Homo_sapiens_assembly38.fasta`).\n- **Variant callers:**\n  - mutect2 and strelka for somatic SNVs and indels\n  - manta for structural variants\n  - haplotypecaller for germline calls on the normal\n- **Other settings:**\n  - Aligner: bwa-mem\n  - wes: false, because this is whole-genome data. The staged GATK calling regions are used.\n  - The pipeline's parameter check passed.\n- **Not available here:** annotation (VEP/snpEff) and copy-number calling (ASCAT/Control-FREEC), because their reference files aren't set up on Luria.\n\n**Run time:** about 8\u201324.5 hours from when the job starts on Luria, plus any time waiting in the queue. Most of that is aligning and calling variants for the 2 whole genomes. This is a rough range, not a promise.\n\nWhen the run finishes, just tell Nessie \"my run is done\" and Nessie will turn the outputs into NExtSEEK upload workbooks for you to review.\n\nIs the pairing right? Reply to confirm, or tell me what to change (callers, aligner, etc.)."
